        "original_id": "3f57d262-2f62-5520-a613-9a5da2a64c60",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Jack and Jill, Paper, Children's Digest\n- Places: New York City\n- Topics: children's magazines, fashion, popular culture, nightlife, music, art, film, magazine publishing\n\nFacts:\n- Children's Digest was originally titled The Children's Digest and was published from October 1950 to May/June 2009.\n- Jack and Jill is an American bimonthly magazine for children aged 7 to 12, and its title comes from the nursery rhyme Jack and Jill.\n- Paper, stylized as PAPER, is an independent magazine based in New York City that focuses on fashion, popular culture, nightlife, music, art, and film.\n- After Children's Digest ceased publication in May/June 2009, it was merged into Jack and Jill by the same publisher.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
